      "title": "std::string Mental Model and Core Operations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "std::string Mental Model and Core Operations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a string is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::string` = `std::basic_string<char>`",
                "==Owns== a contiguous, growable `char` buffer",
                "Tracks **size** and **capacity**",
                "`c_str()` and `data()` are ==null-terminated=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cost of operations",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Operation",
                "Cost",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`size` `[]` `front` `back`",
                  "O(1)",
                  "`[]` out of range = {red:UB}"
                ],
                [
                  "`at(i)`",
                  "O(1)",
                  "throws `out_of_range`"
                ],
                [
                  "`push_back` `append`",
                  "amortised O(1)",
                  "capacity grows geometrically"
                ],
                [
                  "`insert` `erase` (middle)",
                  "O(n)",
                  "tail shifts"
                ],
                [
                  "`find(x)`",
                  "O(n*m) worst",
                  "returns `npos`"
                ],
                [
                  "`substr(pos, len)`",
                  "O(len)",
                  "copies; throws if `pos > size()`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Not found gives ==npos==, not -1 or 0",
                "Compare with `npos`, never with an `int`",
                "`reserve(n)` pre-allocates, avoiding reallocation"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "s.reserve(1000);  // one allocation",
                "auto p = s.find(\"ab\");",
                "if (p == std::string::npos) {",
                "    // not found",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Use `at()` when unsure of the index. `[]` never checks, and `find` answers with `npos`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Small String Optimisation and Memory Layout",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Small String Optimisation and Memory Layout",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What SSO Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==SSO== keeps short strings **inside** the string object, no heap",
                "Limit: ~15 chars libstdc++/MSVC, 22 libc++ (implementation-defined)",
                "Past the limit the string allocates on the ==heap=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::string s;",
                "std::cout << s.capacity();"
              ],
              "note": "empty capacity() reveals the inline limit"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "15"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Moves and Invalidation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Short (SSO)",
                "Long (heap)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Bytes live",
                  "inside object",
                  "on heap"
                ],
                [
                  "`std::move`",
                  "copies inline bytes",
                  "steals pointer, O(1)"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Invalidated by move, swap, growth",
              "items": [
                "Pointers, references, iterators into the string",
                "Never keep them across those operations"
              ],
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rules",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Short strings are ==cache-friendly== and allocation-free",
                "Small keys: take **std::string by value**",
                "`reserve()` matters only past the inline buffer"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What is SSO?** Inline buffer for short strings, no heap",
                "**Is moving a short string a steal?** No, it copies bytes",
                "**Why do iterators die on move?** Inline bytes move with the object"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
