    {
      "title": "std::string_view and Dangling Pitfalls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "std::string_view and Dangling Pitfalls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. View and Parameters",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`string_view` (C++17): ==pointer + length==, **non-owning**",
                "Copy and `substr` are ==O(1)==, no allocation",
                "Takes `std::string`, `const char*`, literals",
                "Read-only params: use it, not `const std::string&`",
                "A literal to `const std::string&` builds a temporary string"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "void show(std::string_view s);",
                "show(\"hello\");  // no temporary string"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How Views Dangle",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cause",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`sv = std::string(\"hi\")`",
                  "temporary freed at `;`"
                ],
                [
                  "Return view of a local",
                  "local dies on return"
                ],
                [
                  "`append`, `reserve`, move",
                  "buffer reallocates"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "std::string_view f() {",
                "  std::string s = \"hi\";",
                "  return s;  // dangles",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Safety Rules",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Not null-terminated",
              "items": [
                "Never pass `sv.data()` to a C API wanting `'\\0'`",
                "Build a `std::string` first",
                "No views as members or in containers unless the owner outlives them"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A view never extends lifetime. Owner dies or grows: ==dangling==."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does a view dangle?** It never owns the buffer",
                "**Why a `string_view` parameter?** Literals need no temporary string",
                "**Is `sv.data()` safe for C APIs?** No, no `'\\0'` guaranteed"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Conversions and String Streams",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Conversions and String Streams",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Number to String",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`std::to_string(n)` takes int, long, double",
                "double always uses ==%f==: `3.14` becomes `3.140000`",
                "{red:Poor for floats}: fixed 6 decimals",
                "Fast and locale-free: `std::to_chars` (`<charconv>`)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. String to Number",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "No digits",
                "Overflow"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`stoi` `stol` `stod`",
                  "`std::invalid_argument`",
                  "`std::out_of_range`"
                ],
                [
                  "`from_chars`",
                  "no throw",
                  "no throw"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "cpp",
              "lines": [
                "size_t pos = 0;",
                "int n = std::stoi(\"12abc\", &pos);",
                "if (pos != 5) { /* junk left */ }",
                "int v;",
                "auto [p, ec] = std::from_chars(b, e, v);",
                "if (ec == std::errc()) { /* ok */ }"
              ],
              "note": "stoi gives 12 silently; check pos"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`from_chars`: fast, non-throwing, ==locale-independent==",
                "Always check ==ec == std::errc()=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. String Streams",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ostringstream`: build with `<<`, read with `.str()`",
                "`istringstream`: parse with `>>` or `std::getline(ss, tok, ',')` to split",
                "Both are slower than `to_string`/`from_chars`: locale and stream overhead"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Reusing a stream",
              "text": "Call `ss.str(\"\")` and `ss.clear()`. A failed extraction leaves error flags set; ==clear()== resets them."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**to_string vs from_chars?** Format vs parse; from_chars is faster, no throw",
                "**stoi(\"12abc\")?** Returns 12; pass `&pos` to detect junk"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
